
                                PYTHON 2.7.18
                                  FOR AMIGA

                              amigazen project


           Original Amiga port (through 2.0) by Irmen de Jong.
    Updated to Python 2.7.18 by amigazen project (continuing that work).
         (Original Python by Guido van Rossum and many others)


                   Read the file Help/DISCL_and_COPYRIGHT !

   It contains the disclaimer for this software, and copyright notices.


	Quick start (no installer)
	~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

	1. Copy this entire drawer anywhere on your hard disk (or a large
	   floppy volume).  Keep the files together.

	2. Double-click the Python icon, or from a Shell type the full
	   path to Python (or add this drawer to your PATH).

	3. Libraries live next to the binary:

		lib/python27.zip
		lib/lib-dynload/
		lib/site-python/

	   No ASSIGN is required when you run Python from this drawer.

	4. Optional convenience (S:User-Startup):

		ASSIGN Python: <path to this drawer>
		PATH Python: ADD

	   Then you can type "Python" from any Shell, and set project
	   icons' Default Tool to Python:Python.


	Contents of this drawer
	~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

	Python              Interpreter (Workbench + Shell)
	Python.help         AmigaDOS Help text for the Python command
	RunTest.py          Regression test launcher
	lib/                Standard library zip, extensions, site-python
	Help/               Guides and Amiga module notes
	  AmigaPython.guide Port documentation (AmigaGuide)
	  DiveIntoPython/   "Dive Into Python" tutorial (AmigaGuide, GFDL)
	  Amiga/            Amiga module notes (reST)
	  DISCL_and_COPYRIGHT  Disclaimer and licenses
	  CHANGES           Amiga port change history
	Demo/               Example scripts (see Demo/readme)
	Icons/              Extra / NewIcon suggestions


	Documentation map
	~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

	* Shell:   Help Python   (or open Python.help)
	* Guide:   Help/AmigaPython.guide
	* Tutorial: Help/DiveIntoPython/DiveIntoPython.guide
	* Language / library reference (upstream):
	  https://docs.python.org/2.7/
	* amigazen project:
	  https://github.com/amigazen/amigapython/
	  http://www.amigazen.com/amigapython/


	Workbench
	~~~~~~~~~

	* Double-click Python for an interactive console window.
	* Project icons: set Default Tool to this Python binary (or
	  Python:Python if you made the ASSIGN).  The project file is
	  passed as the script.
	* Close the console with the window close gadget or Ctrl+C.


	Shell examples
	~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

		Python
		Python script.py
		Python -c "print 'hello'"
		Python -?
		Python -c "import test.pystone; test.pystone.main()"


	Tests and demos
	~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

	* RunTest.py starts the regression suite (needs the test package
	  inside lib/python27.zip).  Some tests skip on Amiga; start a
	  TCP stack before socket tests; usergroup.library for pwd/grp.
	* Demo/ holds Amiga-checked example scripts (see Demo/readme).
	  Try: Python Demo/scripts/beer.py
	       Python Demo/amiga/amiga_info.py



	Troubleshooting
	~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

	* "Python libraries not found"
	  Keep lib/ next to the Python binary, or ASSIGN Python: to this
	  drawer.

	* "Couldn't open bsdsocket.library"
	  Start a TCP stack that provides bsdsocket.library (e.g. Roadshow).
	  I-Net225 is not supported.

	* Math co-processor / CPU messages
	  Use a binary matching your CPU (68020+).  Soft-float builds do
	  not need an FPU.

	* Crashes on deep recursion
	  Increase the stack size on the Python icon or Shell Stack.

	* PIPE: / os.popen oddities
	  Replace the default l:queue-handler (e.g. HWGQueue from Aminet).

	See Docs/AmigaPython.guide for more detail.


	What's new (short)
	~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

	This is Python 2.7.18 for AmigaOS, continuing the classic AmigaPython
	2.0 line.  See Docs/NEWS and CHANGES.  Amiga-specific modules and
	notes are under Docs/Amiga/.


